  "name": "Dirty Blades adds Nature damage and a stacking healing reduction (#6714)",
  "contract": "Dirty Blades (680276) promises Nature damage equal to 70% of each landed melee autoattack, rounded down per hit, and its helper (520571) reduces healing received by 20% per stack up to two stacks. A level-28 Ranger attacks a stunned, lower-level opposing player without Nature resistance outside the protected starting zone. Observe actual white and Nature damage, native two-stack healing reduction and expiry. Pilfering (705087) raises the share to 80% and heals for 50% of actual Nature damage; a Nature-only absorb shield must prevent healing while leaving white swings intact, then removal restores the heal. Each normal Dirty Blades cast starts with the required Advantage aura and 100 Focus; the resource prerequisite is a fixture, not the reported defect. The copied Nature helper preserves the resolved white amount without a second outgoing or target multiplier; independent Nature resists and absorbs still apply. A +400 AP fixture in the final phase makes each swing large enough to distinguish the 80% share despite integer rounding. Apply the existing +400 AP fixture before the 70% sample too. Require at least 40 total white damage for its two-hit sample: less than two points of per-hit truncation then leaves the 70% share above 65%. Keep the original percentage, absorption, healing and expiry assertions.",
